  provenanceNote: 'Registered against Shield as declared by Assets/GalaQuest/Gear/Editor/Fixtures/Registrations/GearAssetFitProfile_gear_shield_ironwood.asset.
    Cavity taken from the authored fit profile for gear.shield.ironwood (AuthoredVirtualCavity):
    AUTHORED functional envelope, not a measured cavity. The source art declares
    no GQ_FIT_CAVITY locator, and a shield encloses no anatomy, so there is no interior
    shell to measure and none is invented here. What is authored is the DECISION
    that this board IS the functional envelope for fit purposes; the extents themselves
    are the board the source mesh presents, in canonical asset space after the raw-to-canonical
    rotation below. Raw-to-canonical is AUTHORED from a human observation about the
    source art: the exported board lies flat, with its thinnest axis on raw +Y, so
    +90 degrees about X stands it upright with its face on canonical +Z (wearer forward).
    The source FBX is also authored at roughly one centimetre across, which is why
    normalization against the Hero produces a large uniform scalar; that is a source
    unit convention, not a fit decision. Fit cavity (0.0100, 0.0100, 0.0017) m gives
    0.0100 m along Up; the Hero requires 0.3233 m, so the single uniform scale is
    32.32719. Outer render bounds (0.0100, 0.0100, 0.0017) m -> (0.3233, 0.3233,
    0.0559) m are used for silhouette checks only. The Owner-authored uniform scale
    for this item is 32.32719; the contract computes 100.0 % of it.'
